                        "glosses": [
                            "A short bat for beating clothes when washing them."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "494edcbe-4962-4739-89d7-3409c780e8b5",
                                "sense_id": "86f90422-281a-37db-93f1-2ef95ba10851",
                                "text": "Clo[wn]. And I mine: I remember when I was in loue, I broke my ſword vpon a ſtone, and bid him take that for comming a night to Iane Smile, and I remember the kiſſing of her batler [var. batlet], and the Cowes dugs that her prettie chopt hands had milk’d; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b5aa7cb-84fa-4ae4-a879-44e982c2cba9",
                                "sense_id": "86f90422-281a-37db-93f1-2ef95ba10851",
                                "text": "These 'batlets', which had of necessity to be made from well-seasoned wood, were evidently prized household items, often intricately carved on the upper surface."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff10ffc6-053a-4996-8606-aa4a5211bd52",
                                "sense_id": "86f90422-281a-37db-93f1-2ef95ba10851",
                                "text": "\"If you come between me and my actions again, I will take a batlet to you.\" He shoved past her so hard that Dougless nearly fell against the wall, and she watched with a heavy heart as he strode angrily down the path and out through the door ..."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
